                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sharia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "589d803f-d8e7-3721-8f9e-192256b6736b",
                                        "entry_id": "4720d592-dcca-355f-9919-a85ac93f2db9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of shari'a."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c038aac3-65ae-4ae3-979e-ec2fa4e77ebd",
                                                "sense_id": "589d803f-d8e7-3721-8f9e-192256b6736b",
                                                "text": "After all, Usamah had served the sadist Zangi and, if read in full, his account presents a picture of Islamic violence no less shocking to modern sensibilities: the collecting of Christian heads, the crucifying and bisections of their own soldiers and heretics, the severe punishments of Islamic sharia – and the story of how his father, in a rage, lopped off the arm of his page."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5dc27e9-376d-4356-b95e-f6c0c1ad91c9",
                                                "sense_id": "589d803f-d8e7-3721-8f9e-192256b6736b",
                                                "text": "Unlike in Somalia, Iraq and Afghanistan, in Yemen they are trying to implement sharia by winning over the hearts and minds of the people."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8b7fc345-a0d9-436e-ab10-8c40f16c2be1",
                        "source_entry_id": "d798dfa6-bd42-33a2-a0ba-b6d1f3891b63",
                        "source_sense_id": "8502d1a7-5cd0-370e-ac3a-e0ee91a34d1a",
                        "source_sense_description": "de islamitische wetgeving",
                        "target_lang_word": "charia",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "charia",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2a63a08-9d07-31b0-a7a8-61b396b6163a",
                                        "entry_id": "73f89dae-6875-3641-a93e-e57619dd6eba",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Loi religieuse islamique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6994f060-e9b8-4c49-a590-745e0536ef60",
                                                "sense_id": "f2a63a08-9d07-31b0-a7a8-61b396b6163a",
                                                "text": "L’islam est la seule religion qui ait logiquement tendu à organiser une société sur ce principe, par le moyen de la charia, moyen qui consolide l’éthique sociale de l’islam, mais laisse de côté la politique, l’administration et le commerce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "546261cf-cb82-4a28-b6b5-0388be95c76e",
                                                "sense_id": "f2a63a08-9d07-31b0-a7a8-61b396b6163a",
                                                "text": "« Si vous dites “la charia” et que vous avez trois musulmans, ils se comporteront comme les partis d'extrême gauche, c'est-à-dire qu'ils vont se diviser en trois petits partis très rapidement ! »"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe90de40-6561-4d6b-b2d3-6a7fa6b443fa",
                                                "sense_id": "f2a63a08-9d07-31b0-a7a8-61b396b6163a",
                                                "text": "D’où la radicalisation des positions, d’où les intolérances, les boucs émissaires, les Saint Barthélemy, les charias, les guerres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96629ade-72fe-4cb2-bdca-e0a3a11a0c18",
                                                "sense_id": "f2a63a08-9d07-31b0-a7a8-61b396b6163a",
                                                "text": "En effet, pour pallier les défaillances de la charia, qui ne fonctionnait pas très bien, Mourad avait instauré un code pénal séculier appelé kanun, destiné à faciliter les poursuites et à rendre la justice plus efficace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
